<title>USA: Plaintiffs' lawyers in Texaco suit ask $29 mln-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Plaintiffs' lawyers in Texaco suit ask $29 mln-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lawyers for plaintiffs in the Texaco Inc racial descrimination lawsuit are asking for fees of some $29 million, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday, citing settlement documents to be filed in court this week.</p>
<p>The story said the attorneys are asking for about 25 percent of the $115 million that Texaco has agreed to pay some current and former black employees.</p>
</text>
